{"id": "EUVD-2026-101223", "enisaUuid": "81c828b9-08b4-3cc5-bc01-0894cdeced4a", "description": "BottleCRM 0.45 through 1.14.5 contains an uncontrolled memory allocation vulnerability in _read_upload() that reads entire CSV uploads before enforcing the 5 MB limit. Authenticated users with mass-import permission can send oversized CSV files concurrently to /api/contacts/import/ and /api/cases/import/ endpoints to exhaust worker memory and trigger out-of-memory termination.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T11:39:01", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Django-CRM/Django-CRM/issues/828", "https://github.com/Django-CRM/Django-CRM/blob/v1.14.5/backend/contacts/import_views.py#L44", "https://github.com/Django-CRM/Django-CRM/blob/v1.14.5/backend/cases/import_views.py#L44", "https://github.com/aaronamran/CVE-Disclosures/tree/main/CVE-2026/CVE-2026-110595", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/bottlecrm-0.45-through-1.14.5-memory-exhaustion-via-contact-and-case-csv-import"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8vqj-3q69-wq28", "CVE-2026-110595"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "888a2876-f3ab-3dd6-9604-cde2802d8e33", "product": {"name": "BottleCRM", "vendor": {"name": "MicroPyramid"}}, "product_version": "0.45 \u22641.14.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a0380927-b6ac-3cb9-838c-9e62ac43ed33", "vendor": {"name": "MicroPyramid"}}], "isExploited": false}